273
00:23:12,105 --> 00:23:14,938
we can truly connect with each other

274
00:23:15,605 --> 00:23:19,605
when we make love.

275
00:23:26,563 --> 00:23:27,813
Yes.

276
00:23:29,480 --> 00:23:32,396
Okay. We'll cancel your appointment.

277
00:23:32,896 --> 00:23:34,605
Take care.

278
00:23:44,813 --> 00:23:45,938
Hello.

279
00:23:46,021 --> 00:23:49,438
-You don't have an appointment.
-Could you fit me in?

280
00:23:49,521 --> 00:23:51,896
From the looks of it,
you don't seem too busy.

281
00:23:51,980 --> 00:23:53,021
Right?

282
00:23:53,105 --> 00:23:55,730
How can you come back here
after writing that article?

283
00:23:55,813 --> 00:23:57,355
It's my job.

284
00:24:00,146 --> 00:24:01,688
Hello, Doctor.

285
00:24:01,771 --> 00:24:02,771
Hello.

286
00:24:03,521 --> 00:24:05,355
It's okay, Natsume.

287
00:24:19,021 --> 00:24:22,105
Humans are strange, aren't they?

288
00:24:23,480 --> 00:24:26,480
Normally, if you experienced
something so horrific,

289
00:24:26,563 --> 00:24:30,188
you'd choose a career
as far removed from it as possible.

290
00:24:30,896 --> 00:24:32,563
But not you, Doctor.

291
00:24:34,896 --> 00:24:38,480
You deliberately chose a job
that deals with sex.

292
00:24:42,355 --> 00:24:43,396
Mr. Kitano.

293
00:24:43,980 --> 00:24:46,480
How have things been
with Wakako since then?

294
00:24:46,563 --> 00:24:47,480
Have you talked--

295
00:24:47,563 --> 00:24:49,396
Wait. Don't tell me…

296
00:24:50,605 --> 00:24:53,230
Did that incident awaken something in you?

297
00:24:53,313 --> 00:24:54,271
Like a sexual fetish?

298
00:24:55,688 --> 00:24:58,771
So you chose a job where you can
peek into other people's sex lives.

299
00:24:58,855 --> 00:24:59,855
I see.

300
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,521
Do you enjoy poking at people's wounds?

301
00:25:04,771 --> 00:25:06,480
-Saikawa.
-I'm offended.

302
00:25:07,938 --> 00:25:10,271
In a way, we're in the same business.

303
00:25:10,355 --> 00:25:12,480
You and me.

304
00:25:13,438 --> 00:25:14,271
Huh?

305
00:25:15,646 --> 00:25:17,938
You dig up people's misfortunes

306
00:25:18,021 --> 00:25:19,688
and make a living off them.

307
00:25:19,771 --> 00:25:21,605
He's nothing like you!

308
00:25:22,105 --> 00:25:24,855
You have no idea
how many people he's helped.

309
00:25:24,938 --> 00:25:26,396
I've seen it firsthand.

310
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:28,855
-Stop it.
-No! This is frustrating!

311
00:25:30,980 --> 00:25:32,855
I used to think the same thing.

312
00:25:32,938 --> 00:25:36,396
That being a sex therapist
was kind of shady.

313
00:25:38,188 --> 00:25:39,438
So I couldn't tell anyone.

314
00:25:40,271 --> 00:25:41,896
Not even my girlfriend.

315
00:25:43,938 --> 00:25:47,813
But do you know how many people
keep their sexual problems to themselves?

316
00:25:48,396 --> 00:25:51,438
I realized how precious it is
to have someone who truly listens

317
00:25:51,521 --> 00:25:54,438
without judging or laughing at you.

318
00:25:54,521 --> 00:25:56,480
-I see.
-Even someone like you…

319
00:25:56,563 --> 00:25:58,688
-Saikawa.
-He still takes you seriously!

320
00:25:58,771 --> 00:26:00,438
That's enough, Saikawa!

321
00:26:04,896 --> 00:26:06,480
You're in front of a client.

322
00:26:07,146 --> 00:26:08,980
Please watch your language.

323
00:26:12,730 --> 00:26:13,730
Sorry.

324
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,855
My apologies.

325
00:26:20,938 --> 00:26:21,771
No. It's fine.

326
00:26:21,855 --> 00:26:23,063
Let's begin.

327
00:26:32,688 --> 00:26:34,146
You were so cool.

328
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:35,521
Please stop.

329
00:26:35,605 --> 00:26:37,688
"No! This is frustrating!"

330
00:26:37,771 --> 00:26:39,188
Seriously, stop it.

331
00:26:39,271 --> 00:26:41,896
Hey, why did you become a nurse?

332
00:26:42,521 --> 00:26:43,688
Where did that come from?

333
00:26:43,771 --> 00:26:45,813
Well, I've never asked before.

334
00:26:45,896 --> 00:26:48,896
I didn't know your family
runs a hospital either.

335
00:26:52,563 --> 00:26:56,188
At first, I wanted to be a soccer player.

336
00:26:56,271 --> 00:26:58,021
Really?

337
00:26:58,105 --> 00:27:01,521
But in high school,
I got seriously injured and gave it up.

338
00:27:02,855 --> 00:27:04,563
When I had surgery at the hospital--

339
00:27:04,646 --> 00:27:05,855
Oh, I know!

340
00:27:06,355 --> 00:27:07,646
You fell for a nurse.

341
00:27:07,730 --> 00:27:09,521
No, that's not it.

342
00:27:11,855 --> 00:27:14,063
Well, I guess you're not too far off.

343
00:27:15,021 --> 00:27:17,980
My older brother was
the smart one in the family.

344
00:27:18,063 --> 00:27:20,230
He's taken over the family hospital.

345
00:27:20,313 --> 00:27:23,938
I was no good at studying.

346
00:27:24,438 --> 00:27:26,855
I was pretty much
the family disappointment.

347
00:27:28,771 --> 00:27:31,021
When I couldn't play soccer anymore

348
00:27:31,105 --> 00:27:32,855
and hit rock bottom,

349
00:27:32,938 --> 00:27:36,188
the only person who encouraged me
was a nurse.

350
00:27:38,896 --> 00:27:42,313
That's when I realized
how amazing nurses are.

351
00:27:43,063 --> 00:27:44,313
I admired them.

352
00:27:45,105 --> 00:27:48,980
Even if I couldn't be a doctor, I thought
I'd make my parents proud as a nurse.

353
00:27:51,855 --> 00:27:55,480
But they said it'd be a disgrace
to have a nurse in a family of doctors.

354
00:27:56,105 --> 00:27:57,896
They were totally against it.

355
00:27:57,980 --> 00:27:59,396
That's tough.

356
00:27:59,896 --> 00:28:02,855
After that, I was over it.

357
00:28:03,438 --> 00:28:05,271
So I ignored them

358
00:28:05,855 --> 00:28:11,771
and ended up becoming a nurse on impulse.

359
00:28:13,230 --> 00:28:15,105
So that's what happened.

360
00:28:15,188 --> 00:28:18,438
Even after becoming a nurse,
I was still unsure of myself.

361
00:28:18,521 --> 00:28:20,396
I had no confidence.

362
00:28:20,896 --> 00:28:22,480
But that's changed now, right?

363
00:28:32,438 --> 00:28:34,521
Sorry. I gotta go.

364
00:28:34,605 --> 00:28:36,480
Huh? Did you forget something?

365
00:28:36,563 --> 00:28:37,646
No.

366
00:28:38,146 --> 00:28:39,396
I've made up my mind.

367
00:28:39,896 --> 00:28:41,521
I'm gonna call my brother.

368
00:28:42,146 --> 00:28:44,563
I'll tell him I decided to work
at Shimotori Clinic.

369
00:28:45,730 --> 00:28:47,688
I never properly told him before.

370
00:28:47,771 --> 00:28:49,771
Yeah? That's great.

371
00:28:51,188 --> 00:28:53,021
The doctor needs me after all.

372
00:28:55,730 --> 00:28:56,730
Good luck.

373
00:28:57,771 --> 00:28:59,438
Good luck!

374
00:29:12,771 --> 00:29:14,563
I said something terrible to him.

375
00:29:16,271 --> 00:29:17,313
I told him,

376
00:29:19,063 --> 00:29:23,063
"I hope that someday we can truly connect
when we make love."

377
00:29:26,855 --> 00:29:27,855
I…

378
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:34,980
unknowingly touched the one wound
he never wanted anyone to touch.

379
00:29:41,063 --> 00:29:45,021
I think he knew
that article was coming out,

380
00:29:45,105 --> 00:29:46,980
so he broke up with me.

381
00:29:48,813 --> 00:29:51,396
He told a clumsy lie
to keep me away from the incident.

382
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:54,105
Ugh. This is so frustrating.

383
00:29:54,605 --> 00:29:57,021
Thinking, "He must've felt this way
when he did that"

384
00:29:57,105 --> 00:30:00,105
or "I don't deserve to do that"…

385
00:30:00,188 --> 00:30:03,438
Oh. This isn't me speaking as a therapist.

386
00:30:03,521 --> 00:30:05,355
It's just my personal opinion.

387
00:30:06,980 --> 00:30:07,980
Okay.

388
00:30:12,230 --> 00:30:15,605
Being considerate
can be a beautiful thing.

389
00:30:16,188 --> 00:30:17,813
But if you truly love him,

390
00:30:18,896 --> 00:30:24,396
you have to step in prepared to get hurt,
and even to hurt him.

391
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:27,063
Otherwise, you'll never grow any closer.

392
00:30:36,355 --> 00:30:38,188
What happened that day

393
00:30:38,688 --> 00:30:41,188
involved you too, didn't it?

394
00:30:58,355 --> 00:31:01,646
"Seventeen years ago, on September 23rd."

395
00:31:02,563 --> 00:31:05,271
"At a small shrine in Kanagawa Prefecture,

396
00:31:06,188 --> 00:31:10,605
the annual lantern festival
was being held."

397
00:32:35,396 --> 00:32:36,230
Huh?

398
00:32:45,230 --> 00:32:46,646
I want you to tell me…

399
00:32:49,688 --> 00:32:51,063
what happened to you

400
00:32:51,938 --> 00:32:53,938
on the day of the festival.

401
00:32:54,855 --> 00:32:56,188
Tell me everything.

402
00:33:03,813 --> 00:33:05,438
It's just as the article said.

403
00:33:06,521 --> 00:33:08,896
I want to hear <i>your </i>excuse.

404
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:15,771
I waited…

405
00:33:18,480 --> 00:33:20,188
until the festival was over.

406
00:33:27,605 --> 00:33:29,688
You stood me up.

407
00:33:30,396 --> 00:33:34,396
Then you transferred schools,
and I never saw you again.

408
00:33:36,396 --> 00:33:38,605
Why did you never come?

409
00:33:39,605 --> 00:33:42,105
Even as an adult,
I kept thinking about it.

410
00:33:47,730 --> 00:33:50,146
You kept me waiting for 17 years.

411
00:33:52,271 --> 00:33:53,480
At least

412
00:33:54,730 --> 00:33:56,730
let me hear your excuse.

413
00:34:09,271 --> 00:34:10,480
That day…

414
00:34:13,230 --> 00:34:14,646
I went there too.

415
00:34:15,813 --> 00:34:16,771
To the shrine.

416
00:34:37,813 --> 00:34:38,646
<i>But then…</i>

417
00:34:38,730 --> 00:34:39,646
DAD

418
00:34:39,730 --> 00:34:41,396
<i>…my father called.</i>

419
00:34:42,771 --> 00:34:46,188
-Hello?
-<i>His voice sounded desperate.</i>

420
00:34:46,271 --> 00:34:47,146
What?

421
00:34:47,646 --> 00:34:49,021
<i>He said my mother was gone…</i>

422
00:34:49,105 --> 00:34:50,021
Okay.

423
00:34:50,105 --> 00:34:52,063
<i>…and told me to hurry home.</i>

424
00:35:08,938 --> 00:35:12,855
<i>My father said we were going</i>
<i>to look for my mother.</i>

425
00:35:15,271 --> 00:35:18,855
But it seemed like
he already knew where she was.

426
00:35:30,105 --> 00:35:31,021
We're here.

427
00:35:52,646 --> 00:35:54,021
Whose house is this?

428
00:35:54,605 --> 00:35:56,146
Can we really just go in?

429
00:36:01,855 --> 00:36:02,855
Ichito.

430
00:36:05,063 --> 00:36:06,396
Take a good look.

431
00:36:52,980 --> 00:36:53,980
Stop.

432
00:36:55,396 --> 00:36:56,313
Stop…

433
00:36:57,063 --> 00:36:58,646
Please, stop!

434
00:37:25,563 --> 00:37:27,188
<i>My mother was always</i>

435
00:37:28,438 --> 00:37:31,855
kind and devoted to our family.

436
00:37:34,855 --> 00:37:35,855
<i>I thought</i>

437
00:37:37,396 --> 00:37:39,813
<i>we were an ideal family.</i>

438
00:37:49,105 --> 00:37:51,855
The reason I became a sex therapist…

439
00:37:54,605 --> 00:37:56,938
is because I hate sex.

440
00:38:01,021 --> 00:38:03,271
I saw something meant to express love…

441
00:38:05,396 --> 00:38:07,855
destroy people's lives.

442
00:38:11,605 --> 00:38:14,230
When I first studied sexology
in medical school,

443
00:38:15,438 --> 00:38:16,521
I thought, "Oh,

444
00:38:17,688 --> 00:38:21,730
sex could be understood logically,"
and I felt relieved.

445
00:38:26,771 --> 00:38:32,063
I thought if I could treat it
as knowledge rather than emotion,

446
00:38:33,855 --> 00:38:36,688
I could make sense of my aversion.

447
00:38:38,105 --> 00:38:39,105
But…

448
00:38:41,896 --> 00:38:43,313
I still…

449
00:38:57,063 --> 00:39:00,480
Where… are your parents now?

450
00:39:06,355 --> 00:39:09,355
My father went to prison.

451
00:39:11,313 --> 00:39:13,855
I don't know where he went
after he was released.

452
00:39:16,646 --> 00:39:18,021
My mother…

453
00:39:20,438 --> 00:39:22,188
is apparently in a care facility.

454
00:39:23,438 --> 00:39:24,688
"Apparently"?

455
00:39:29,438 --> 00:39:31,105
I haven't seen her at all.

456
00:39:34,313 --> 00:39:36,438
My father's family took me in.

457
00:39:38,605 --> 00:39:39,730
And ever since…

458
00:39:47,605 --> 00:39:48,813
Why…

459
00:39:51,563 --> 00:39:53,771
did my father go that far?

460
00:39:56,230 --> 00:39:57,646
Why

461
00:39:58,646 --> 00:40:00,563
did my mother betray us?

462
00:40:01,938 --> 00:40:03,605
I still don't know.

463
00:40:09,855 --> 00:40:12,480
She seemed so happy.

464
00:40:12,563 --> 00:40:13,813
Let's go see her.

465
00:40:15,313 --> 00:40:16,313
What?

466
00:40:19,063 --> 00:40:20,688
I'll go with you.

467
00:40:24,105 --> 00:40:25,521
If you don't see her,

468
00:40:26,605 --> 00:40:28,646
you'll never understand

469
00:40:30,396 --> 00:40:31,688
your mother.

470
00:42:46,771 --> 00:42:48,688
Subtitle translation by: Yuki Asami

